            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0208" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/400–401.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Lorillard to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-10-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 30, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 446.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s instruction
                    No. 160 of March 10, 1908, inviting the Government of Portugal to take part in a
                    joint investigation of the opium trade and the opium habit in the Far East, and
                    in continuation of Mr. Bryan’s No. 422 of August 4, 1908, on the same subject, I
                    have the honor to inclose herewith a copy and a translation of a note from the
                    foreign office, dated the 22d instant, whereby the Portuguese Government
                    officially accepts the invitation of the American Government, states its
                    intention to be represented on the international commission which is to meet at
                    Shanghai in January next, and adds that the subject to be discussed has been the
                    object of investigation by a committee sitting at Macau since August last.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George
                    Lorrillard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d96-a1.xml" xpointer="d96-a1"/>
            </div>
